Grafana Data Sources

🔹 What are Data Sources? 📊
A data source is the system from which Grafana retrieves data for visualization.
Grafana itself does not store monitoring data.
Instead, it connects to external systems and displays their data through dashboards.
👉 Think of it this way:
📦 Data Source → Stores Data
 📊 Grafana → Visualizes Data

🔹 Why are Data Sources Important? 🏗️
Without data sources, Grafana has nothing to display.
They enable:
✔ Real-time monitoring
 ✔ Historical analysis
 ✔ Performance tracking
 ✔ Business insights

🔹 Prometheus Connection 🔗
The most common Grafana integration is with Prometheus.
How it works:
1️⃣ Prometheus collects metrics
 2️⃣ Stores metrics as time-series data
 3️⃣ Grafana queries Prometheus
 4️⃣ Dashboards display the results
Examples:
📊 CPU Usage
 📊 Memory Usage
 📊 Request Rate
 📊 Error Rate
This combination is one of the most widely used monitoring stacks in modern DevOps environments.

